  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Food Security, Livelihoods and Resilience in Syria EH</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Action contributes to the economic self -reliance and resilience building of conflict -affected communities in Rural Damascus and Deir Ez Zor governorates. As such, it directly contributes to the achievement of the Overall Objective &quot;to address early recovery, resilience and self -reliance needs of Syrian communities and local agents for change in Syria&quot; of European Union (EU) Special Measures for Syria . It also directly improves the livelihood opportunities of Syrian communities affected by chronic instability. Moreover, by providing access to viable opportunities and promoting sustainable growth across four selected value chains (wheat, fodder, dairy products, vegetables), the Action will ultimately improve resilience, food security, and livelihoods. The proposed activities are also aligned with the indicative activities, specifically regarding the Resilience building of smallholders&apos; crop and livestock production through Climate Smart Agriculture. Provision of vocational skill training; Geographical focus on North -eastern Syria and community level resilience. The Action is also aligned with the main messages that emerged from the VI Brussels Conference (2022) on &quot;supporting the future of Syria and the Region&quot;, especially when it comes to &quot;stepping up early recovery efforts [&#x2026;] to support resilience, community capacity building, and self -reliance through the participatory provision of basic services, livelihoods, and local economic development&quot; (point 27); and ensure aid delivery to &quot;all Syrians in need, wherever they are and as long as needed&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
